[I] Tensor library for machine learning

[T] ggml is a low-level, cross-platform tensor library for machine learning,
[T] used by llama.cpp and whisper.cpp. It supports integer quantization,
[T] broad hardware backends, automatic differentiation and ADAM/L-BFGS
[T] optimizers, without third-party dependencies and with zero memory
[T] allocations at runtime.

[U] https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml

[A] GGML Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/development
